          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Culture</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Working at MEAICON.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>MEAICON is an engineering company first and a services company second. The people who succeed here are the ones who want to own the outcome — not hand off a ticket, not escalate a problem they could solve, not blame the vendor when the architecture they designed fails. We hire for ownership, technical depth, and operational judgement, and we back that with a culture that treats engineering decisions as the most important decisions in the company.</p>
          <p>You will work on infrastructure that governments, banks, hospitals, and telecom operators depend on every hour of every day. The work is real. The stakes are real. The accountability is real. But so is the reward — there is no distance between the architecture you draw and the system you operate. You see it through, from design to 3am incident response, and the lessons compound with every engagement.</p>
          <p>Growth at MEAICON is not a ladder — it is depth. Our engineers do not specialise narrowly and plateau. They work across connectivity, data centre, cybersecurity, blockchain, and cloud, building cross-stack expertise that makes them more valuable with every project. You will work across eleven markets spanning the GCC, Africa, South Asia, and North America, with exposure to diverse regulatory frameworks, technology stacks, and operational environments. The region is our lab, and the work is meaningful.</p>
          <p>We invest in our people because our people are the product. Certification programmes, vendor training, cross-market rotations, and direct access to the leadership team — not because it sounds good in a careers page, but because the quality of our delivery is directly determined by the quality of our team. If you want to build and operate systems that matter, this is where to do it.</p>
        </div>
